<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Limit of a Function at a Given Point</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Find \(\displaystyle \lim_{x \rightarrow {@aa@}} {@fx@}\)</p>
<p><em>Note: If no limit exists, give <code>NO</code> as your answer.</em></p>
<p>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>
<p>[[feedback:prt1]] </p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>

<p>To find \(\lim_{x \rightarrow {@aa@}} {@fx@}\), we can simplify the expression and substitute \(x = {@aa@}\) into the simplified expression.</p>

<p>First, let's simplify the expression. The common factor in the numerator and denominator cancel out.</p>
<p style="margin-left: 30px">\(\displaystyle
{@fx@} = \frac{({@(cc*x-bb)@})\times({@(x-aa)@})}{{@(x-aa)@}} = {@(cc*x-bb)@}
\)</p>

<p>Now, we can substitute \(x = {@aa@}\) into the expression.</p>
<p hidden>{@simp:false;@}
<p style="margin-left: 30px">\(\begin{align*}
\displaystyle \lim_{x \rightarrow {@aa@}} {@fx@}
\displaystyle &= \lim_{{x\to {@aa@}}} ({@(cc*x-bb)@}) \\ 
\displaystyle &= {@line1@}  \\
\displaystyle &= {@line2@} \\
\displaystyle &= {@ta@}\
\end{align*}\)</p>
<p hidden>{@simp:true;@}

<p>Therefore, \( \displaystyle \lim_{x \rightarrow {@aa@}} {@fx@} = {@ta@}\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
